ed to SQLite via DataRowService (create, update, delete, fetch by templateId)\",\n   237→        \"Build succeeds with zero errors\"\n   238→      ],\n   239→      \"description\" : \"As a user, I want to add, duplicate, and delete data rows in the spreadsheet grid and edit cell values inline so that I can manage multiple sets of variable values for a template.\",\n   240→      \"id\" : \"US-014\",\n   241→      \"inProgress\" : false,\n   242→      \"passes\" : false,\n   243→      \"priority\" : 14,\n   244→      \"title\" : \"Build data grid with row CRUD and inline editing\"\n   245→    },\n   246→    {\n   247→      \"acceptanceCriteria\" : [\n   248→        \"Right preview pane displays the rendered prompt as plain text (no markdown\\/rich text rendering)\",\n   249→        \"Clicking a data row selects it and updates the preview with the prompt rendered using that row's values\",\n   250→        \"When no data row is selected, the preview renders the template with uppercase placeholder values (e.g., {{user_name}} becomes USER_NAME)\",\n   251→        \"Empty required fields in the selected row are shown as highlighted placeholders in the preview\",\n   252→        \"Preview updates in real time as cell values are edited (no explicit refresh needed)\",\n   253→        \"A Copy button at the top of the preview pane copies the rendered prompt to the system clipboard\",\n   254→        \"After copying, a brief Copied toast\\/overlay is displayed for 1.5 seconds\",\n   255→        \"Build succeeds with zero errors\"\n   256→      ],\n   257→      \"description\" : \"As a user, I want the preview pane to show the rendered prompt for the selected data row (or placeholders when no row is selected) and copy the result to clipboard so that I can quickly generate and use prompts.\",\n   258→      \"id\" : \"US-015\",\n   259→      \"inProgress\" : false,\n   260→      \"passes\" : false,\n   261→      \"priority\" : 15,\n   262→      \"title\" : \"Build preview pane with rendered prompt, placeholder fallback, and copy\"\n   263→    },\n   264→    {\n   265→      \"acceptanceCriteria\" : [\n   266→        \"Template body changes trigger an auto-save after a 500ms debounce (no save while user is actively typing)\",\n   267→        \"Auto-save calls TemplateService.update to persist the template\",\n   268→        \"After a successful save, VersionService.createSnapshot is called to create a new version snapshot\",\n   269→        \"Title and description changes also trigger auto-save with the same debounce, but do NOT create version snapshots\",\n   270→        \"Data row cell edits trigger auto-save of the DataRow with the same debounce\",\n   271→        \"No manual Save button is needed; all saves are automatic\",\n   272→        \"Build succeeds with zero errors\"\n   273→      ],\n   274→      \"description\" : \"As a user, I want my template changes to be saved automatically after I stop typing so that I never lose work, and each save creates a version snapshot for history.\",\n   275→      \"id\" : \"US-016\",\n   276→      \"inProgress\" : false,\n   277→      \"passes\" : false,\n   278→      \"priority\" : 16,\n   279→      \"title\" : \"Implement auto-save with debounce and version snapshots\"\n   280→    },\n   281→    {\n   282→      \"acceptanceCriteria\" : [\n   283→        \"A Version History button or menu item opens a version history panel\\/sheet for the selected template\",\n   284→        \"The panel displays a chronological list of versions: version number, timestamp (relative format), and optional note\",\n   285→        \"Selecting a version displays its full template body in a read-only text view\",\n   286→        \"A Restore button creates a new version with the selected version's body (non-destructive) and updates the template editor to show the restored content\",\n   287→        \"User can add or edit a note on any version via an inline text field or popover\",\n   288→        \"The version list refreshes after a restore to show the newly created version at the top\",\n   289→        \"Build succeeds with zero errors\"\n   290→      ],\n   291→      \"description\" : \"As a user, I want to view a chronological list of version snapshots for a template, view any previous version in read-only mode, and restore it so that I can iterate on templates without fear of losing previous work.\",\n   292→      \"id\" : \"US-017\",\n   293→      \"inProgress\" : false,\n   294→      \"passes\" : false,\n   295→      \"priority\" : 17,\n   296→      \"title\" : \"Build version history list with read-only viewer and restore\"\n   297→    },\n   298→    {\n   299→      \"acceptanceCriteria\" : [\n   300→        \"In the version history panel, user can select two versions for comparison (e.g., via checkboxes or shift-click)\",\n   301→        \"A Compare button opens a diff view showing the two versions side by side\",\n   302→        \"Added lines\\/text are highlighted in green; deleted lines\\/text are highlighted in red\",\n   303→        \"The diff view shows version numbers and timestamps for both versions as headers\",\n   304→        \"User can dismiss the diff view to return to the version list\",\n   305→        \"Diff algorithm handles multi-line templates correctly (line-level diff, not character-level)\",\n   306→        \"Build succeeds with zero errors\"\n   307→      ],\n   308→      \"description\" : \"As a user, I want to select any two versions and view a side-by-side diff with additions and deletions highlighted so that I can understand what changed between iterations.\",\n   309→      \"id\" : \"US-018\",\n   310→      \"inProgress\" : false,\n   311→      \"passes\" : false,\n   312→      \"priority\" : 18,\n   313→      \"title\" : \"Build side-by-side diff comparison view\"\n   314→    },\n   315→    {\n   316→      \"acceptanceCriteria\" : [\n   317→        \"Right-clicking a template shows an Export... context menu item\",\n   318→        \"Export serializes the template, its data rows, and version snapshots into a single JSON file using Codable\",\n   319→        \"Export presents a NSSavePanel defaulting to ~\\/Documents with filename [template-title].json\",\n   320→        \"File > Import (or a toolbar button) presents an NSOpenPanel to select a .json file\",\n   321→        \"Import deserializes the JSON and checks for duplicate template IDs in the local database\",\n   322→        \"If a duplicate is found, an alert presents three options: Skip, Overwrite, or Import as Copy\",\n   323→        \"Import as Copy creates a new template with a new UUID and (Copy) appended to the title\",\n   324→        \"Invalid or malformed JSON shows a user-facing error with error code (using PromptyError.importFailed)\",\n   325→        \"Build succeeds with zero errors\"\n   326→      ],\n   327→      \"description\" : \"As a user, I want to export a template (with its data rows, version history, and referenced partials) as a JSON file and import JSON files with duplicate detection so that I can share templates with others.\",\n   328→      \"id\" : \"US-019\",\n   329→      \"inProgress\" : false,\n   330→      \"passes\" : false,\n   331→      \"priority\" : 19,\n   332→      \"title\" : \"Implement single template export and import with duplicate detection\"\n   333→    },\n   334→    {\n   335→      \"acceptanceCriteria\" : [\n   336→        \"Settings window is accessible via Cmd+, (standard macOS Settings shortcut) and the app menu\",\n   337→        \"Settings are organized into sections: General, Editor, Export\\/Import, Advanced\",\n   338→        \"General section includes: Default folder (dropdown of existing folders + Uncategorized), Auto-save debounce interval (stepper, ms, default 500), Multi-line variable suffix (text field, default _text)\",\n   339→        \"Editor section includes: Font size (stepper, pt, default 13), Tab width (stepper, spaces, default 4)\",\n   340→        \"Export\\/Import section includes: Default export directory (path picker, default ~\\/Documents), Batch copy delimiter (text field, default newline-dash-newline)\",\n   341→        \"Advanced section includes: Debug Mode toggle (default off)\",\n   342→        \"Settings are persisted using @AppStorage (UserDefaults) and take effect immediately\",\n   343→        \"Build succeeds with zero errors\"\n   344→      ],\n   345→      \"description\" : \"As a user, I want a settings window where I can configure editor preferences, export defaults, and debug mode so that I can customize the app to my workflow.\",\n   346→      \"id\" : \"US-020\",\n   347→      \"inProgress\" : false,\n   348→      \"passes\" : false,\n   349→      \"priority\" : 20,\n   350→      \"title\" : \"Build settings panel\"\n   351→    },\n   352→    {\n   353→      \"acceptanceCriteria\" : [\n   354→        \"File menu includes: New Template (Cmd+N), New Folder (Cmd+Shift+N), Import (Cmd+I), Export (Cmd+E), Close (Cmd+W)\",\n   355→        \"Edit menu includes standard items: Undo, Redo, Cut, Copy, Paste, Select All (provided by SwiftUI)\",\n   356→        \"View menu includes: Toggle Sidebar (Cmd+Option+S), Toggle Preview (Cmd+Option+P), Toggle Template Editor, Toggle Data Interface\",\n   357→        \"A Copy Rendered Prompt shortcut (Cmd+Shift+C) copies the current preview to clipboard regardless of focus\",\n   358→        \"All menu items are enabled\\/disabled appropriately based on context (e.g., Export disabled when no template is selected)\",\n   359→        \"Menu items use .commands modifier on the WindowGroup or Scene\",\n   360→        \"Build succeeds with zero errors\"\n   361→      ],\n   362→      \"description\" : \"As a user, I want standard macOS menu bar menus and keyboard shortcuts for all primary actions so that I can work efficiently without reaching for the mouse.\",\n   363→      \"id\" : \"US-021\",\n   364→      \"inProgress\" : false,\n   365→      \"passes\" : false,\n   366→      \"priority\" : 21