pple Silicon with the standard folder layout so that all subsequent stories have a consistent codebase structure.\",\n      \"id\" : \"US-001\",\n      \"inProgress\" : true,\n      \"passes\" : false,\n      \"priority\" : 1,\n      \"title\" : \"Set up Xcode project with SwiftUI scaffold and folder structure\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\" : [\n        \"GRDB.swift (or SQLite.swift) added as a Swift Package dependency\",\n        \"Template model with fields: id (UUID), title (String), description (String?), body (String), folderId (UUID?), createdAt (Date), updatedAt (Date)\",\n        \"Folder model with fields: id (UUID), name (String), createdAt (Date), updatedAt (Date)\",\n        \"DataRow model with fields: id (UUID), templateId (UUID, foreign key), values (JSON-encoded dictionary [String: String]), createdAt (Date)\",\n        \"VersionSnapshot model with fields: id (UUID), templateId (UUID, foreign key), versionNumber (Int), body (String), note (String?), createdAt (Date)\",\n        \"Database initializer creates all tables with proper foreign keys and indexes on templateId\",\n        \"Database file is stored at ~\\/Library\\/Application Support\\/Prompty\\/prompty.db\",\n        \"Build succeeds with zero errors\"\n      ],\n      \"description\" : \"As a developer, I want the core data models and SQLite schema defined so that persistence services can read and write templates, folders, data rows, and version snapshots.\",\n      \"id\" : \"US-002\",\n      \"inProgress\" : false,\n      \"passes\" : false,\n      \"priority\" : 2,\n      \"title\" : \"Define data models and SQLite schema\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\" : [\n        \"MustacheService class in Services\\/ with two public methods: extractVariables(from template: String) -> [String] and render(template: String, with values: [String: String]) -> String\",\n        \"extractVariables returns unique variable names in order of first appearance, extracted from {{variableName}} tags\",\n        \"render replaces {{variableName}} with the corresponding value from the dictionary\",\n        \"Variables not present in the values dictionary are replaced with their uppercase name (e.g., {{user_name}} becomes USER_NAME)\",\n        \"Empty string values are treated as provided (not replaced with placeholder)\",\n        \"Unit tests cover: simple variables, multiple variables, duplicate variables, missing variables (placeholder fallback), empty values, special characters in values, templates with no variables\",\n        \"Build succeeds with zero errors\"\n      ],\n      \"description\" : \"As a developer, I want a Mustache parsing and rendering service so that templates can be parsed for variable extraction and rendered with data values or placeholders.\",\n      \"id\" : \"US-003\",\n      \"inProgress\" : false,\n      \"passes\" : false,\n      \"priority\" : 3,\n      \"title\" : \"Implement Mustache parser and renderer service\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\" : [\n        \"TemplateService class in Services\\/ with methods: create, fetchAll, fetchById, fetchByFolderId, update, delete\",\n        \"create generates a UUID, sets createdAt\\/updatedAt, inserts into SQLite, and returns the new Template\",\n        \"update sets updatedAt to current time\",\n        \"delete removes the template and cascades to delete associated DataRow and VersionSnapshot records\",\n        \"All methods use GRDB's DatabaseQueue for thread-safe access\",\n        \"Unit tests cover: create, fetch, update, delete, fetch by folder, cascade delete\",\n        \"Build succeeds with zero errors\"\n      ],\n      \"description\" : \"As a developer, I want a service to create, read, update, and delete templates in SQLite so that the UI layer can manage templates without direct database access.\",\n      \"id\" : \"US-004\",\n      \"inProgress\" : false,\n      \"passes\" : false,\n      \"priority\" : 4,\n      \"title\" : \"Implement template CRUD persistence service\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\" : [\n        \"FolderService class in Services\\/ with methods: create, fetchAll, rename, delete\",\n        \"delete accepts a strategy parameter: .moveToUncategorized (sets folderId = nil on contained templates) or .deleteContents (deletes contained templates and their associated data)\",\n        \"fetchAll returns folders sorted by name\",\n        \"Unit tests cover: create, fetch all, rename, delete with move strategy, delete with cascade strategy\",\n        \"Build succeeds with zero errors\"\n      ],\n      \"description\" : \"As a developer, I want a service to create, read, update, and delete folders in SQLite so that templates can be organized into collections.\",\n      \"id\" : \"US-005\",\n      \"inProgress\" : false,\n      \"passes\" : false,\n      \"priority\" : 5,\n      \"title\" : \"Implement folder CRUD persistence service\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\" : [\n        \"VersionService class in Services\\/ with methods: createSnapshot, fetchVersions(for templateId), restore(versionId, for templateId)\",\n        \"createSnapshot saves the current template body as a new VersionSnapshot with an auto-incremented versionNumber\",\n        \"fetchVersions returns snapshots ordered by versionNumber descending (newest first)\",\n        \"restore creates a new snapshot (with the restored body) rather than overwriting — non-destructive restore\",\n        \"updateNote(versionId, note) method allows adding\\/editing a note on a snapshot\",\n        \"Unit tests cover: create snapshot, fetch versions ordering, restore creates new version, update note, multiple snapshots for same template\",\n        \"Build succeeds with zero errors\"\n      ],\n      \"description\" : \"As a developer, I want a service to manage version snapshots so that every template save creates a snapshot and users can list, view, and restore previous versions.\",\n      \"id\" : \"US-006\",\n      \"inProgress\" : false,\n      \"passes\" : false,\n      \"priority\" : 6,\n      \"title\" : \"Implement version history persistence service\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\" : [\n        \"PromptyError enum in Models\\/ with cases for common errors: .templateParseFailed, .databaseWriteFailed, .databaseReadFailed, .exportFailed, .importFailed, .invalidTemplate, .folderDeleteFailed\",\n        \"Each case has a unique error code string (e.g., PRM-1001, PRM-2001) and a human-readable summary\",\n        \"Errors include a context property with details (what failed, which template\\/folder, suggested action)\",\n        \"Errors distinguish between user-correctable (e.g., malformed template) and internal failures (e.g., database error)\",\n        \"ErrorPresenter utility that formats error code + summary + context into a copyable string\",\n        \"Each error string is unique and greppable to locate the exact throw site in source\",\n        \"Unit tests verify each error case produces a unique code and non-empty summary\",\n        \"Build succeeds with zero errors\"\n      ],\n      \"description\" : \"As a developer, I want a centralized error handling framework so that all user-facing errors display a summary, unique error code, and a Copy error details button.\",\n      \"id\" : \"US-007\",\n      \"inProgress\" : false,\n      \"passes\" : false,\n      \"priority\" : 7,\n      \"title\" : \"Implement error handling framework\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\" : [\n        \"ContentView uses NavigationSplitView or equivalent to create three panes: sidebar (left), center, preview (right)\",\n        \"Center pane is a vertical VSplitView with two sections: template editor (top) and data interface (bottom)\",\n        \"Left sidebar has a toggle button to show\\/hide it\",\n        \"Right preview pane has a toggle button to show\\/hide it\",\n        \"Template editor section in the center pane has a collapse\\/expand disclosure control\",\n        \"Data interface section in the center pane has a collapse\\/expand disclosure control\",\n        \"All panes use semantic\\/adaptive system colors for backgrounds and borders (light\\/dark mode compatible)\",\n        \"Build succeeds with zero errors\"\n      ],\n      \"description\" : \"As a user, I want a three-pane window layout (sidebar, center, preview) so that I can navigate templates, edit them, and see the preview simultaneously.\",\n      \"id\" : \"US-008\",\n      \"inProgress\" : false,\n      \"passes\" : false,\n      \"priority\" : 8,\n      \"title\" : \"Build three-pane app shell layout\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\" : [\n        \"Sidebar displays an All Templates item at the top that is always visible\",\n        \"Below All Templates, user-created folders are listed alphabetically\",\n        \"A + button in the sidebar toolbar creates a new folder with an inline text field for naming\",\n        \"Right-clicking a folder shows a context menu with Rename and Delete options\",\n        \"Rename makes the folder name editable inline\",\n        \"Delete shows an alert asking the user to choose: Move templates to Uncategorized or Delete templates\",\n        \"Selecting a folder filters the template list to that folder; selecting All Templates shows all\",\n        \"Sidebar uses List with selection binding to track the selected folder\",\n        \"Build succeeds with zero errors\"\n      ],\n      \"description\" : \"As a user, I want to see my folders in the sidebar and create, rename, and delete them so that I can organize my templates into collections.\",\n      \"id\" : \"US-009\",\n      \"inProgress\" : false,\n      \"passes\" : false,\n      \"priority\" : 9,\n      \"title\" : \"Build sidebar with folder list and folder management\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\" : [\n        \"Each template list row displays: title (primary text), description snippet (secondary text, truncated