,\n      \"inProgress\" : false,\n      \"passes\" : false,\n      \"priority\" : 11,\n      \"title\" : \"Build sidebar search\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\" : [\n        \"Center pane top section shows three fields: title (single-line TextField), description (single-line TextField, optional), and body (multi-line TextEditor)\",\n        \"The body editor applies syntax highlighting to Mustache {{variable}} tags using a distinct color (e.g., system accent color) that contrasts with plain text in both light and dark mode\",\n        \"Standard macOS text editing works: undo\\/redo, cut\\/copy\\/paste, select all\",\n        \"Body field has no artificial maximum length\",\n        \"Changes to title, description, or body are reflected in the view model immediately (bound via @Binding or @Published)\",\n        \"Build succeeds with zero errors\"\n      ],\n      \"description\" : \"As a user, I want a template editor with title, description, and body fields where Mustache {{variable}} tags are visually highlighted so that I can author templates with clear variable markers.\",\n      \"id\" : \"US-012\",\n      \"inProgress\" : false,\n      \"passes\" : false,\n      \"priority\" : 12,\n      \"title\" : \"Build template editor view with syntax highlighting\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\" : [\n        \"DataGridViewModel observes changes to the template body and calls MustacheService.extractVariables to get the current variable list\",\n        \"Data grid columns are generated from the extracted variables, in order of first appearance in the template\",\n        \"When a new variable is added to the template, a new column appears in the data grid\",\n        \"When a variable is removed from the template, its column is removed from the data grid (existing cell data for that variable is preserved in the DataRow.values dictionary but hidden from view)\",\n        \"Duplicate variable references in the template produce only one column\",\n        \"Column headers display the variable name formatted for readability (e.g., user_name becomes User Name)\",\n        \"Build succeeds with zero errors\"\n      ],\n      \"description\" : \"As a user, I want the data grid columns to automatically update when I add or remove Mustache variables in the template body so that the spreadsheet always matches the current template.\",\n      \"id\" : \"US-013\",\n      \"inProgress\" : false,\n      \"passes\" : false,\n      \"priority\" : 13,\n      \"title\" : \"Build variable extraction and data grid column generation\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\" : [\n        \"Data interface section in the center pane displays a table\\/grid with one column per variable and one row per DataRow\",\n        \"An Add Row button below the grid creates a new empty DataRow for the current template\",\n        \"Right-clicking a row shows a context menu with Duplicate Row and Delete Row\",\n        \"Duplicate Row creates a new DataRow with the same values as the selected row\",\n        \"Cells support inline text editing — clicking a cell makes it editable\",\n        \"Required variables (all variables by default) show a visual flag (e.g., red border or highlight) when the cell is empty\",\n        \"Rows with any empty required fields show a warning indicator on the row\",\n        \"Data rows are persisted to SQLite via DataRowService (create, update, delete, fetch by templateId)\",\n        \"Build succeeds with zero errors\"\n      ],\n      \"description\" : \"As a user, I want to add, duplicate, and delete data rows in the spreadsheet grid and edit cell values inline so that I can manage multiple sets of variable values for a template.\",\n      \"id\" : \"US-014\",\n      \"inProgress\" : false,\n      \"passes\" : false,\n      \"priority\" : 14,\n      \"title\" : \"Build data grid with row CRUD and inline editing\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\" : [\n        \"Right preview pane displays the rendered prompt as plain text (no markdown\\/rich text rendering)\",\n        \"Clicking a data row selects it and updates the preview with the prompt rendered using that row's values\",\n        \"When no data row is selected, the preview renders the template with uppercase placeholder values (e.g., {{user_name}} becomes USER_NAME)\",\n        \"Empty required fields in the selected row are shown as highlighted placeholders in the preview\",\n        \"Preview updates in real time as cell values are edited (no explicit refresh needed)\",\n        \"A Copy button at the top of the preview pane copies the rendered prompt to the system clipboard\",\n        \"After copying, a brief Copied toast\\/overlay is displayed for 1.5 seconds\",\n        \"Build succeeds with zero errors\"\n      ],\n      \"description\" : \"As a user, I want the preview pane to show the rendered prompt for the selected data row (or placeholders when no row is selected) and copy the result to clipboard so that I can quickly generate and use prompts.\",\n      \"id\" : \"US-015\",\n      \"inProgress\" : false,\n      \"passes\" : false,\n      \"priority\" : 15,\n      \"title\" : \"Build preview pane with rendered prompt, placeholder fallback, and copy\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\" : [\n        \"Template body changes trigger an auto-save after a 500ms debounce (no save while user is actively typing)\",\n        \"Auto-save calls TemplateService.update to persist the template\",\n        \"After a successful save, VersionService.createSnapshot is called to create a new version snapshot\",\n        \"Title and description changes also trigger auto-save with the same debounce, but do NOT create version snapshots\",\n        \"Data row cell edits trigger auto-save of the DataRow with the same debounce\",\n        \"No manual Save button is needed; all saves are automatic\",\n        \"Build succeeds with zero errors\"\n      ],\n      \"description\" : \"As a user, I want my template changes to be saved automatically after I stop typing so that I never lose work, and each save creates a version snapshot for history.\",\n      \"id\" : \"US-016\",\n      \"inProgress\" : false,\n      \"passes\" : false,\n      \"priority\" : 16,\n      \"title\" : \"Implement auto-save with debounce and version snapshots\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\" : [\n        \"A Version History button or menu item opens a version history panel\\/sheet for the selected template\",\n        \"The panel displays a chronological list of versions: version number, timestamp (relative format), and optional note\",\n        \"Selecting a version displays its full template body in a read-only text view\",\n        \"A Restore button creates a new version with the selected version's body (non-destructive) and updates the template editor to show the restored content\",\n        \"User can add or edit a note on any version via an inline text field or popover\",\n        \"The version list refreshes after a restore to show the newly created version at the top\",\n        \"Build succeeds with zero errors\"\n      ],\n      \"description\" : \"As a user, I want to view a chronological list of version snapshots for a template, view any previous version in read-only mode, and restore it so that I can iterate on templates without fear of losing previous work.\",\n      \"id\" : \"US-017\",\n      \"inProgress\" : false,\n      \"passes\" : false,\n      \"priority\" : 17,\n      \"title\" : \"Build version history list with read-only viewer and restore\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\" : [\n        \"In the version history panel, user can select two versions for comparison (e.g., via checkboxes or shift-click)\",\n        \"A Compare button opens a diff view showing the two versions side by side\",\n        \"Added lines\\/text are highlighted in green; deleted lines\\/text are highlighted in red\",\n        \"The diff view shows version numbers and timestamps for both versions as headers\",\n        \"User can dismiss the diff view to return to the version list\",\n        \"Diff algorithm handles multi-line templates correctly (line-level diff, not character-level)\",\n        \"Build succeeds with zero errors\"\n      ],\n      \"description\" : \"As a user, I want to select any two versions and view a side-by-side diff with additions and deletions highlighted so that I can understand what changed between iterations.\",\n      \"id\" : \"US-018\",\n      \"inProgress\" : false,\n      \"passes\" : false,\n      \"priority\" : 18,\n      \"title\" : \"Build side-by-side diff comparison view\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\" : [\n        \"Right-clicking a template shows an Export... context menu item\",\n        \"Export serializes the template, its data rows, and version snapshots into a single JSON file using Codable\",\n        \"Export presents a NSSavePanel defaulting to ~\\/Documents with filename [template-title].json\",\n        \"File > Import (or a toolbar button) presents an NSOpenPanel to select a .json file\",\n        \"Import deserializes the JSON and checks for duplicate template IDs in the local database\",\n        \"If a duplicate is found, an alert presents three options: Skip, Overwrite, or Import as Copy\",\n        \"Import as Copy creates a new template with a new UUID and (Copy) appended to the title\",\n        \"Invalid or malformed JSON shows a user-facing error with error code (using PromptyError.importFailed)\",\n        \"Build succeeds with zero errors\"\n      ],\n      \"description\" : \"As a user, I want to export a template (with its data rows, version history, and referenced partials) as a JSON file and import JSON files with duplicate detection so that I can share templates with others.\",\n      \"id\" : \"US-019\",\n      \"inProgress\" : false,\n      \"passes\" : false,\n      \"priority\" : 19,\n      \"title\" : \"Implement single template export and import with duplicate detection\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\" : [\n        \"Settings window is accessible via Cmd+, (standard macOS Settings shortcut) and the app menu\",\n        \"Settings are organized into sections: General, Editor, Export\\/Import, Advanced\",\n        \"General section includes: Default folder (dropdown of existing folders + Uncategorized), Auto-save debounce interval (stepper, ms, default 500), Multi-line variable suffix (text field, default _text)\",\n        \"Editor section includes: Font size (stepper, pt, default 13), Tab width (stepper, spaces, default 4)\",\n        \"Export\\/Import section includes: Default export directory (path picker, default ~\\/Documents), Batch copy delimiter (text field, default newline-dash-newline)\",\n        \"Advanced section includes: Debug Mode toggle (default off)\",\n        \"Settings are persisted using @AppStorage (UserDefaults) and take effect immediately\",\n        \"Build succeeds with zero errors\"\n      ],\n      \"description\" : \"As a user, I want a settings window where I can configure editor preferences, export defaults, and debug mode so that I can customize the app to my workflow.\",\n      \"id\" : \"US-020\",\n      \"inProgress\" : false,\n      \"passes\" : false,\n      \"priority\" : 20,\n      \"title\" : \"Build settings panel\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\" : [\n        \"File menu includes: New Template (Cmd+N), New Folder (Cmd+Shift+N), Import (Cmd+I), Export (Cmd+E), Close (Cmd+W)\",\n        \"Edit menu includes standard items: Undo, Redo, Cut, Copy, Paste, Select All (provided by SwiftUI)\",\n        \"View menu includes: Toggle Sidebar (Cmd+Option+S), Toggle Preview (Cmd+Option+P), Toggle Template Editor, Toggle Data Interface\",\n        \"A Copy Rendered Prompt shortcut (Cmd+Shift+C) copies the current preview to clipboard regardless of focus\",\n        \"All menu items are enabled\\/disabled appropriately based on context (e.g., Export disabled when no template is selected)\",\n        \"Menu items use .commands modifier on the WindowGroup or Scene\",\n        \"Build succeeds with zero errors\"\n      ],\n      \"description\" : \"As a user, I want standard macOS menu bar menus and keyboard shortcuts for all primary actions so that I can work efficiently without reaching for the mouse.\",\n      \"id\" : \"US-021\",\n      \"inProgress\" : false,\n      \"passes\" : false,\n      \"priority\" : 21,\n      \"title\" : \"Implement menu bar and keyboard shortcuts\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\" : [\n        \"LoggingService in Services\\/ wraps os.Logger with a consistent subsystem and category naming convention (e.g., subsystem: com.prompty.app, categories: persistence, mustache, ui)\",\n        \"All log calls use structured key-value format with template ID, operation name, and timing where applicable\",\n        \"Log severity levels used consistently: .debug for verbose internals, .info for normal operations, .warning for recoverable issues, .error for failures\",\n        \"When Debug Mode is enabled in Settings, a debug info pane appears showing: selected template ID, parsed variable list, last render timing (ms), recent log entries\",\n        \"Debug pane updates in real time as the user interacts with the app\",\n        \"Debug pane is completely hidden when Debug Mode is off\",\n        \"Build succeeds with zero errors\"\n      ],\n      \"description\" : \"As a developer, I want structured logging via os.Logger and a debug mode pane so that issues can be diagnosed from logs or from the in-app debug view.\",\n      \"id\" : \"US-022\",\n      \"inProgress\" : false,\n      \"passes\" : false,\n      \"priority\" : 22,\n      \"title\" : \"Implement structured logging and debug mode pane\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\" : [\n        \"All custom colors use semantic\\/adaptive NSColor values (e.g., Color(.labelColor), Color(.textBackgroundColor), Color(.separatorColor)) — no hardcoded color literals\",\n        \"Mustache syntax highlighting color is readable in both light and dark mode\",\n        \"Preview pane text, data grid cells, sidebar items, and error dialogs all use adaptive colors\",\n        \"All borders and dividers use Color(.separatorColor) or equivalent\",\n        \"Window position, size, pane proportions (sidebar width, preview width, editor\\/data split), and collapsed states are saved using @SceneStorage or UserDefaults\",\n        \"On relaunch, the window restores to its previous position, size, and pane configuration\",\n        \"The previously selected template is re-selected on relaunch\",\n        \"Build succeeds with zero errors\"\n      ],\n      \"description\" : \"As a user, I want all UI elements to be clearly readable in both light and dark mode, and I want the app to remember my window layout between sessions.\",\n      \"id\" : \"US-023\",\n      \"inProgress\" : false,\n      \"passes\" : false,\n      \"priority\" : 23,\n      \"title\" : \"Light\\/dark mode theming pass and window state restoration\"\n    }\n  ]\n}","numLines":405,"startLine":1,"totalLines":405}}}
